WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:03.919
We all have fond memories of the playground.

00:00:03.919 --> 00:00:10.010
Hours upon hours spent in blissful childhood
abandon, racing around the local park, climbing

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:15.980
the monkey bars, and seeing if you could get
even higher on the swings than your best friend.

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:18.990
And then, of course, there’s the slide.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:20.990
Who doesn’t love a slide?

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:26.130
Only you and the force of gravity pulling
you down through a straight or a spiral tube.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:30.570
Those few seconds of excitement, that rush
of not knowing whether you’ll come out the

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:35.090
other end of the slide or not, that’s enough
of a thrill for any kid.

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:38.590
Of course, you would always come tumbling
out of the mouth of the slide every time,

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:43.640
at worst, with an odd but innocent friction
burn on your leg or arm.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:48.360
But what if, one day, you didn’t come out
of the other end?

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:53.430
Or worse, what if the place at the end of
the slide wasn’t the world you left behind

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:55.280
when you slid through the entrance?

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.530
It doesn’t seem all that likely to happen,
right?

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:06.041
Well, you’ve obviously never taken a trip
down SCP-1562, better known as the Tunnel

00:01:06.041 --> 00:01:07.229
Slide.

00:01:07.229 --> 00:01:12.270
As its moniker suggests, SCP-1562 is a slide.

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:15.840
Or, it at least appears to be an ordinary
tunnel slide.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:20.840
You know, the kind you would easily find at
any kids’ park, jungle gym, or indoor play

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:21.840
area.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:25.789
Just over two meters high and almost three
and a half meters long.

00:01:25.789 --> 00:01:29.909
And for the most part, it is a completely
normal slide.

00:01:29.909 --> 00:01:34.590
If you were to just sit in it and glide down
it, feet first, nothing would happen.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:41.799
Then again, if SCP-1562 was an ordinary, everyday
piece of a playground, then the SCP Foundation

00:01:41.799 --> 00:01:44.499
would not have such a vested interest in it.

00:01:44.499 --> 00:01:50.859
They definitely wouldn’t be keeping it locked
up in quarantine, secured in Testing Lab 46-V

00:01:50.859 --> 00:01:56.810
of Site 24 - and if any Foundation agents
ask, you didn’t hear that from us, by the

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:57.810
way.

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:02.409
The door to the lab is kept locked at all
times, no member of personnel is even allowed

00:02:02.409 --> 00:02:07.460
near the slide unless granted special clearance
to do so by Foundation researcher, Doctor

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.460
Carver.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.340
So, what is it that makes this thing so special?

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:17.400
Well, for one, SCP-1562 was first recovered
by the Foundation from a defunct, abandoned

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.400
playground.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:22.560
The location of this playground has been redacted,
but it was known to be on the outskirts of

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:26.620
a town where a number of young children had
been reported missing.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:31.840
Does SCP-1562 contain some sort of clue as
to where these children were taken?

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:36.610
Perhaps some piece of forensic evidence left
behind by a child-snatching anomaly from another

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:37.840
dimension?

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:39.400
Not quite.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:44.180
SCP-1562 is the thing that took those children.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:48.530
You see, the slide’s anomalous properties
require very specific circumstances in order

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:49.930
to activate.

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:53.360
Like we mentioned earlier, if you were just
sitting on your butt while you were sliding

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:56.200
down it, you would escape unscathed.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:57.640
Laying flat on your back?

00:02:57.640 --> 00:02:59.660
That is also a safe option.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:04.170
Even flailing yourself about, spinning and
rolling and waving your arms, changing position

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:08.219
on the way down would mean that nothing anomalous
would appear to happen.

00:03:08.219 --> 00:03:14.760
However, if someone enters SCP-1562 and travels
down in head first, laying on their stomach

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:20.689
with their arms tucked at their side, almost
in a plank position, then that is when strange

00:03:20.689 --> 00:03:22.909
things start to happen.

00:03:22.909 --> 00:03:27.310
That is when a person finds out what happened
to those missing children.

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:31.770
Only about fifteen centimeters from the opening
of the slide, a person sliding down on their

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:39.140
front, head first, with arms by their sides,
will disappear right before exiting SCP-1562.

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:45.150
In an instant, they will simply be gone, no
longer in the slide or even relocated to anywhere

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:46.209
nearby.

00:03:46.209 --> 00:03:51.120
To make matters worse, every single person
that this has happened to has never been found

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:52.129
again.

00:03:52.129 --> 00:03:55.659
They literally have vanished off the face
of the Earth.

00:03:55.659 --> 00:03:59.170
Unfortunately, there isn’t much that can
be done to prevent this.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:03.569
During testing, the Foundation quickly learned
that tethering a safety line to a subject

00:04:03.569 --> 00:04:06.269
does little to stop them from disappearing.

00:04:06.269 --> 00:04:10.390
They cannot be pulled back from wherever it
is that the slide sends them.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:14.719
The rope they are attached to is simply cut
and goes slack from the moment that a person

00:04:14.719 --> 00:04:16.389
is taken by the slide.

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:19.769
Now, that sounds like the whole story, right?

00:04:19.769 --> 00:04:25.800
Children are going missing, and the Foundation
learns it’s because of SCP-1562, some kind

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:29.000
of interdimensional portal within a playground
slide.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:33.889
So, they acquire the slide, take it away and
keep it locked up securely where it can’t

00:04:33.889 --> 00:04:37.160
cause any more disappearances, end of story.

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:39.620
Except that’s not quite the end.

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:44.610
No, the one thing it’s still possible to
do once someone has disappeared down the slide

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:47.539
is to stay in contact with them.

00:04:47.539 --> 00:04:52.210
The SCP Foundation has expended a number of
test subjects by sending them sliding down

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:56.900
SCP-1562, just to learn what’s on the other
side.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:59.000
Just where does the slide take them?

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:04.199
Luckily, tests like this are precisely what
the Foundation has D Class personnel for.

00:05:04.199 --> 00:05:08.680
So, what happened when the Foundation sent
some D-Classes on a one-way joyride down the

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:09.680
slide?

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:16.831
Well, one test involved a D-Class designated
D-2445, who disappeared into SCP-1562 but

00:05:16.831 --> 00:05:22.590
was given a two-way radio to communicate directly
with Doctor Darritz, one of the research staff.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:28.190
D-2445 reported that he found himself in a
small, cramped tunnel, and quickly requested

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:30.139
to be let back out.

00:05:30.139 --> 00:05:35.320
Doctor Darritz had neglected to tell D-2445
that was impossible, and that no one ever

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:37.449
came back from inside the slide.

00:05:37.449 --> 00:05:41.970
While it was too dark to see anything, the
prisoner described still being laid on his

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:46.780
front but feeling like there were rocks or
dirt surrounding him on all sides.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:52.220
Realizing that he barely had enough room to
move, or even lift his head, D-2445 again

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:56.330
requested to be let out of SCP-1562.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:06:00.599
As the unfortunate D-Class grew increasingly
more unsettled by the movement-restricting

00:06:00.599 --> 00:06:05.639
environment, Doctor Darritz revealed that
the lifeline tethering D-2445 back to the

00:06:05.639 --> 00:06:09.850
Foundation had been severed upon their disappearance
into the slide.

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:15.720
Panicking, D-2445 managed to move forward
slightly and realized that his head had hit

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:17.600
something: a shoe.

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:20.099
A tiny, child’s shoe.

00:06:20.099 --> 00:06:25.129
Communication with D-2445 was called to a
halt, and the Foundation’s researchers discussed

00:06:25.129 --> 00:06:28.080
possible ways they could retrieve the prisoner.

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:32.770
Although most of them probably knew at this
point that this task was likely impossible,

00:06:32.770 --> 00:06:38.479
this test may have taken place before the
Foundation realized that return from SCP-1562

00:06:38.479 --> 00:06:39.910
was impossible.

00:06:39.910 --> 00:06:43.760
The plan was that another D-Class would be
sent into the slide.

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:48.289
Once again, they would be attached to a tether
line and be carrying video and audio recording

00:06:48.289 --> 00:06:52.199
equipment, along with a GPS tracker, and a
headlamp.

00:06:52.199 --> 00:06:57.610
Reaching out to D-2445, Doctor Darritz relayed
this plan to him.

00:06:57.610 --> 00:07:03.250
D-2445 immediately begged to be set free from
SCP-1562, as the doctor attempted to calm

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:06.800
him down, but to little effect.

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:12.879
Something had scared him, truly terrified
him, a sound coming from somewhere within

00:07:12.879 --> 00:07:14.099
the tunnel.

00:07:14.099 --> 00:07:18.319
“It started talking” D-2445 claimed.

00:07:18.319 --> 00:07:22.479
When Doctor Darritz asked for clarity, the
D-Class replied, saying that a little boy

00:07:22.479 --> 00:07:26.860
had tried to speak to him, but that the child
had made little sense.

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:30.729
“He just kept asking where he was, and I
told him I didn't know.

00:07:30.729 --> 00:07:34.319
But I don't think he was really talking to
me, because he didn't respond to my voice,

00:07:34.319 --> 00:07:37.610
and he told me to stop crying when I was actually
sort of calm.”

00:07:37.610 --> 00:07:42.759
When asked if this child had moved at all,
D-2445 said that he was unsure.

00:07:42.759 --> 00:07:47.159
“He started screaming and I told him to
shut up but he just kept screaming and crying

00:07:47.159 --> 00:07:48.780
and asking for his mommy.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:54.240
Then he finally stopped, and shortly after
that, you contacted me again.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:55.379
Please get me out now.”

00:07:55.379 --> 00:08:01.210
Doctor Darrtiz tried to reassure the man,
to little avail, and communication with D-2445

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:05.010
was cut off after he claimed something was
wrong with his chest.

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:10.479
Shortly after the Foundation lost communication
with D-2445, another member of D Class was

00:08:10.479 --> 00:08:12.800
sent into the slide after him.

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:18.470
This subject, referred to officially as D-8600,
had been specifically selected for this task

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:20.780
thanks to his small stature.

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:26.259
Doctor Darrtiz and the other Foundation researchers
testing SCP-1562 believed that the man’s

00:08:26.259 --> 00:08:31.060
thinner body type would allow D-8600 to better
navigate the tunnel that the slide seemed

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:33.140
to transport people to.

00:08:33.140 --> 00:08:36.260
And you can probably guess what happened next.

00:08:36.260 --> 00:08:41.469
Just like all the others that had been sent
down the slide, D-8600 was trapped.

00:08:41.469 --> 00:08:45.600
His lifeline was cut the moment that he vanished
inside the tunnel slide.

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:50.420
On top of this, the GPS tracker that this
thinner D Class had been issued with seemed

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:52.649
to not be working properly.

00:08:52.649 --> 00:08:57.260
Its signal could not be correctly traced,
and without an accurate fix, there was no

00:08:57.260 --> 00:09:04.040
way to determine the location to which SCP-1562
was transporting its victims - if it was even

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:05.380
in this universe.

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:10.800
Additionally, the video feed to the camera
D-8600 was carrying also failed to connect,

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:15.130
with only audio from his radio being recovered
by the research team.

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:20.380
Contacting D-8600, Doctor Darritz was informed
by this new D Class that his headlamp had

00:09:20.380 --> 00:09:25.010
stopped working the second he had arrived
in the same cave or tunnel as earlier test

00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:26.320
subjects.

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:32.160
Before long, by shimmying through the area
on his arms, D-8600 bumped into a foot, believed

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:33.510
to be belonging to D-2445.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:41.380
While he could barely see anything, D-8600
could hear D-2445’s voice, and this was

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:43.720
being faintly picked up via his radio.

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:48.580
However, as he and Doctor Darritz tried to
talk to the first prisoner, his words began

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:50.200
to sound all too familiar.

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:51.200
“I don't know.

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:53.160
Some sort of very small tunnel.

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:54.200
It's really cramped.

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:55.250
Can you get me out now?”

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:57.370
followed by “No, it's too dark.

00:09:57.370 --> 00:09:59.850
I can't see anything, and I'm stuck.”

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:07.930
It was all just a recording of what D-2445
had said when he’d first arrived after SCP-1562

00:10:07.930 --> 00:10:10.450
had sent him into the tunnel.

00:10:10.450 --> 00:10:15.940
D-8600 did not realize this at first and attempted
to help his fellow prisoner, hoping to pull

00:10:15.940 --> 00:10:18.550
him out of wherever they were trapped.

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:23.260
Doctor Darritz tried desperately to explain
that D-2445 was just repeating his half of

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:28.079
an earlier conversation, but D-8600 hardly
noticed that was the case.

00:10:28.079 --> 00:10:32.550
He gripped the other D Class’ ankles and
told the doctor to pull them out of the tunnel.

00:10:32.550 --> 00:10:37.540
The doctor revealed that once again the tether
line had been severed, but D-8600 refused

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:39.910
to believe that escape was impossible.

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:45.430
He tried to worm his way back the way he had
come, leaving D-2445 still repeating his words

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:46.430
from earlier.

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:50.010
“He just kept asking where he was, and I
told him I didn't know.

00:10:50.010 --> 00:10:53.240
But I don't think he was really talking to
me, because he didn't respond to my voice,

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:56.380
and he told me to stop crying when I was actually
sort of calm…

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:58.140
I don't think so.

00:10:58.140 --> 00:11:01.959
He started screaming and I told him to shut
up but he just kept screaming and crying and

00:11:01.959 --> 00:11:03.420
asking for his mommy.

00:11:03.420 --> 00:11:07.990
Then he finally stopped, and shortly after
that, you contacted me again.

00:11:07.990 --> 00:11:11.779
Please get me out now…Please hurry, my chest
is really starting to hurt.”

00:11:11.779 --> 00:11:18.320
After yelling at him to stop talking multiple
times, D-8600 noted that D-2445 had finally

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:19.660
gone quiet.

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:23.880
The D Class also remarked that the air was
starting to taste stale, and hoped that there

00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:26.500
would be enough oxygen for him to get back.

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:32.680
Then, just like his predecessor, communication
with D-8600 came to an abrupt stop.

00:11:32.680 --> 00:11:37.899
Doctor Darritz was no longer able to reach
him on the radio, there was nothing but static.

00:11:37.899 --> 00:11:42.260
The Foundation was unable to re-establish
contact with either of the two D Class personnel

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:48.980
lost inside SCP-1562, and any future testing
of the Tunnel Slide was suspended.

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:53.959
To this day, none of us know what exactly
happened to the victims of the tunnel slide.

00:11:53.959 --> 00:11:55.480
Where were they taken?

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:57.230
What had taken them?

00:11:57.230 --> 00:12:01.220
What was making the prior victims repeat their
ominous words?

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:05.540
As horror author Stephen King once put it,
“It’s the unanswered question that stays

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:07.180
with us the longest.”

00:12:07.180 --> 00:12:11.180
But the next time you decide to thrill your
inner child by taking a jaunt to your local

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:14.350
kiddie park, you may just find out for yourself…

00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:21.010
Now go check out “SCP-3001 - Red Reality”
and “Trapped in a Game - SCP-1733 - Season

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:26.180
Opener” for more horrifying anomalous places
you’d really hate to be trapped inside!

